        "created_at": "2013-03-31T04:18:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Evening fellow sentinels,</p><p>I just unpackaged and shuffled the shiny new Rook City cards into the enhanced set box. However, yesterday I was in a few rounds of awesome games with the fellows on the Google+ site, and the randomiser kept bringing up decks I have no access to (especially promos like Ambuscade and Unity). Those I can't really do anything about until the next paycheck, but I did get a brief taste of some of the other expansion pack decks and they all look really interesting.</p><p>Correct me if I'm wrong, but the Infernal Relics heroes feel very much like support casters for other heroes, while the Shattered Timelines heroes are far more straightforward in damage dealing (Omnitron, I'm looking at YOU). Ideally, I'd just get both right out the gate, but that's not really so much an option for me; I can only get one or the other. Does anyone have any suggestions on which to gun for first?</p><p>(It's worse when you also factor in the villains, because as villains Gloomweaver and the Ennead were really, really fun to fight and take down. Arrgh!)</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:50.468Z",
