        "id": 57202,
        "name": "Amnachaidh",
        "username": "Amnachaidh",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-31T12:52:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If you enjoy play complexity - which I do - IR is a great expansion.&nbsp; The Enead is my favorite villain deck to date.&nbsp; ST is just all cylinders, though. If you enjoy play complexity - which I do - IR is a great expansion.&nbsp; The Enead is my favorite villain deck to date.&nbsp; Argent Adept and Nightmist are cool heroes that stretch the boundaries of how hero decks work.</p><p>If Absolute Zero is your favorite EE hero, IR might be your next purchase.</p><p>That said, I would recommend picking up ST first - if for no other reason, to enjoy the current buzz in the forums. I find the heroes uniformly good, the villains compelling, and the environments really fun. ChronoRanger &amp; OmniX are just solid heroes who are going to contribute, probably not dominate, and rarely be totally sidelined.</p>",
